WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:02.180
Gwyn, Lord of Sunlight

00:00:02.180 --> 00:00:04.180
was the first Lord of Light

00:00:04.840 --> 00:00:09.300
He feared the darkness, feared what it would do to his Age of Fire.

00:00:10.120 --> 00:00:13.160
So he surrounded himself with powerful allies.

00:00:13.160 --> 00:00:17.560
Even splitting his own soul, so that their power could be greater.

00:00:18.200 --> 00:00:20.520
They would all fail him in the end.

00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:22.940
Most abandoned the kingdom.

00:00:22.940 --> 00:00:24.180
One went mad.

00:00:24.180 --> 00:00:27.380
Another tried to relight the First Flame

00:00:27.380 --> 00:00:31.540
But none compared to the treachery of the Four Kings

00:00:31.540 --> 00:00:36.020
The Four Kings, who ruled over New Londo, were praised for their foresight.

00:00:36.020 --> 00:00:40.220
Yet still they succumbed to the temptations of the Abyss

00:00:40.220 --> 00:00:46.080
In exchange for the art of Lifedrain, the Four Kings gave up their kingdoms to Dark.

00:00:46.080 --> 00:00:52.340
These were the events of long, long ago, and today no one remembers the kings' names

00:00:52.340 --> 00:01:00.080
However, names change but the story remains the same and four kings again lose their kingdoms to the Abyss.

00:01:01.380 --> 00:01:04.900
One of the four is Vendrick, the present Lord of Light

00:01:05.080 --> 00:01:10.040
Like Gwyn before him, Vendrick surrounded himself with allies he trusted

00:01:10.040 --> 00:01:14.680
He favoured simple warriors, who staked their every battle on strength alone

00:01:14.680 --> 00:01:17.680
and he valued knowledge of all things

00:01:17.680 --> 00:01:24.400
"My lord made magnificent findings on souls, an accomplishment for the ages."

00:01:24.400 --> 00:01:30.740
"He vanquished the four Great Ones and built this kingdom upon their souls."

00:01:30.740 --> 00:01:36.460
"Our King has watched over this land since ages long, long ago."

00:01:36.860 --> 00:01:39.200
The man who was born to rule.

00:01:39.200 --> 00:01:43.880
When he heard that the Giants from across the sea held a threat to his kingdom,

00:01:43.880 --> 00:01:46.740
he vanquished them and claimed their strength.

00:01:46.740 --> 00:01:50.280
When the Iron Kingdom fell, Vendrick sent his soldiers

00:01:50.280 --> 00:01:54.140
to claim the replete stores of iron held in Brume Tower.

00:01:54.140 --> 00:01:57.440
And when the Undead curse threatened his own kingdom,

00:01:57.440 --> 00:02:01.500
Vendrick created monstrosities in the name of the greater good.

00:02:01.500 --> 00:02:04.620
Everything he did, he did for his kingdom.

00:02:04.620 --> 00:02:10.480
To serve him, the King had two he valued above all others, Raime and Velstadt.

00:02:10.500 --> 00:02:14.340
These men were known as the Left and Right Arms of the King.

00:02:14.340 --> 00:02:17.460
Even though they were as different as night and day.

00:02:17.700 --> 00:02:21.420
Raime, the darker brother, cared deeply for his king.

00:02:21.420 --> 00:02:26.460
He sought the man's admiration and saw Vendrick as a regal father-figure.

00:02:26.460 --> 00:02:32.240
His greatshield was emblazoned with a great raven, an omen of death, but it was Raime's favourite bird.

00:02:32.280 --> 00:02:39.080
This greatshield would one day be the only thing left of him in Drangleic, a foreshadowing of his fate.

00:02:39.560 --> 00:02:44.040
Velstadt, the Right Arm of the King, was always at Vendrick's side,

00:02:44.040 --> 00:02:46.300
as if he were his Lord's own shadow.

00:02:46.420 --> 00:02:50.220
They say Drangleic is no place for any cleric with ambition.

00:02:50.420 --> 00:02:52.580
Yet Velstadt had risen to the top

00:02:52.580 --> 00:02:56.660
and remained the exception to his Lord's disregard of miracles.

00:02:57.280 --> 00:03:02.260
The lore tells us that Velstadt was lured to Drangleic from a far away land

00:03:02.260 --> 00:03:04.380
but forgot even why he came.

00:03:04.380 --> 00:03:08.280
You can trace the man's origins to the sunken kingdom of Shulva

00:03:08.280 --> 00:03:13.840
Where even now, amongst the ruins, a wrathful queen summons a follower in his image.

00:03:13.840 --> 00:03:16.040
Such was his loyalty.

00:03:16.040 --> 00:03:20.620
This queen brought destruction to her people and to her King.

00:03:20.620 --> 00:03:26.740
She rose to power by gaining favor with the King and by singing to the ancient dragon they worshipped.

00:03:26.860 --> 00:03:31.740
When the King of Shulva realised her true nature, it was already too late.

00:03:31.740 --> 00:03:35.840
The ancient dragon awoke and spewed poison over the entire city

00:03:35.840 --> 00:03:40.020
until only Elana, the Squalid Queen, remained.

00:03:40.240 --> 00:03:42.660
If Velstadt is indeed from Shulva,

00:03:42.660 --> 00:03:46.800
one has to wonder how he didn't see history repeating itself.

00:03:47.300 --> 00:03:51.380
For the Darkness was rising, and his King was in danger.

00:03:51.900 --> 00:03:55.480
Elana was not the only Child of Dark seeking a King.

00:03:55.480 --> 00:04:01.500
A woman named Nashandra arrived in Drangleic and began courting the current King.

00:04:02.060 --> 00:04:08.100
"She warned Our Lord of the looming threat across the seas, of the Giants."

00:04:08.400 --> 00:04:14.560
"The King crossed the ocean and defeated the Giants with the Queen at his side."

00:04:14.700 --> 00:04:18.860
There was no better way to seduce Vendrick, and the Queen knew it.

00:04:18.860 --> 00:04:24.400
He valued this kingdom above all else and would vanquish any enemy to keep it safe.

00:04:24.660 --> 00:04:26.100
So one has to ask:

00:04:26.100 --> 00:04:32.660
Were the Giants ever a threat? Or were they simply a target Nashandra used to gain Vendrick's trust?

00:04:32.800 --> 00:04:38.480
Regardless, Vendrick conquered the Giants' homeland and counted the battle as won.

00:04:38.820 --> 00:04:42.860
"The Queen brought peace to this land and to her king"

00:04:44.020 --> 00:04:45.660
"A peace so deep..."

00:04:46.180 --> 00:04:47.540
"...it was like..."

00:04:48.820 --> 00:04:50.180
"...the Dark."

00:04:51.600 --> 00:04:54.320
A man can be judged by the company he keeps

00:04:54.320 --> 00:04:57.140
and the company Vendrick kept was loyal indeed.

00:04:57.360 --> 00:05:02.500
Velstadt, the Royal Aegis, would follow his King into darkness, if need be.

00:05:02.500 --> 00:05:07.540
But there is a difference between loyalty to a King and loyalty to a kingdom.

00:05:07.540 --> 00:05:11.580
So only one saw Nashandra for what she truly was,

00:05:11.580 --> 00:05:14.820
while the other was blinded by faith.

00:05:14.820 --> 00:05:16.320
Raime.

00:05:18.440 --> 00:05:24.220
Raime was denounced as a traitor for speaking for his kingdom, but against the King and Queen.

00:05:24.220 --> 00:05:30.960
Velstadt, utterly faithful towards the crown, would vanquish Raime for daring to question the monarchy.

00:05:31.140 --> 00:05:35.780
So the Two Arms of the King clashed, instead of facing the true threat.

00:05:36.020 --> 00:05:42.020
Nashandra had eliminated any threats to the kingdom, and had found a King blinded by love.

00:05:42.020 --> 00:05:46.880
She was perfectly poised to usurp the throne, and Raime saw it.

00:05:47.140 --> 00:05:52.500
The King's tragic flaw was his pride and Velstadt's flaw was his mindless faith.

00:05:52.820 --> 00:05:57.060
For without tolerating those who challenge us, how can we grow?

00:05:57.060 --> 00:06:03.120
The Light is always moving forward, and the Darkness will only win when the Light stops seeking it out.

00:06:03.220 --> 00:06:09.860
With the kingdom at peace, Nashandra had halted the kingdom's momentum and Darkness crept closer.

00:06:10.240 --> 00:06:14.480
Velstadt should have recognised the pattern that took place long ago in Shulva.

00:06:14.480 --> 00:06:18.220
Both of his Kings were being manipulated by a Child of Dark.

00:06:18.220 --> 00:06:21.720
Yet Velstadt did nothing to stop it happening again.

00:06:21.940 --> 00:06:26.120
His faith in his King was absolute. The truth, irrelevant.

00:06:26.120 --> 00:06:30.560
The King valued strength and loyalty, and both were on display here.

00:06:30.560 --> 00:06:34.560
Velstadt fought for his King, Raime for the fate of his kingdom.

00:06:34.620 --> 00:06:37.100
Both were loyal, both were powerful.

00:06:37.400 --> 00:06:39.620
Yet Velstadt was the victim.

00:06:40.700 --> 00:06:44.140
Raime was not killed for his treason, he was exiled.

00:06:44.140 --> 00:06:49.400
His strength had not been enough, so he left the kingdom in search of greater strength.

00:06:49.400 --> 00:06:50.860
He would never return.

00:06:51.500 --> 00:06:55.880
He had learned that being right is meaningless without power to back it up.

00:06:55.880 --> 00:07:00.300
Anyone could see that the kingdom was deteriorating under Nashandra's rule.

00:07:00.300 --> 00:07:03.580
Yet Velstadt's faith had overpowered the truth.

00:07:03.940 --> 00:07:07.480
Velstadt had come from a kingdom where a Dark Queen remained.

00:07:07.480 --> 00:07:11.840
So perhaps Raime set out to check if other kingdoms had suffered the same fate?

00:07:12.260 --> 00:07:15.220
So it was that he found himself in Brume Tower

00:07:15.220 --> 00:07:19.160
A place that had once belonged to the Iron King before his fall.

00:07:19.920 --> 00:07:23.240
It was common knowledge that the Iron King had taken no Queen.

00:07:23.240 --> 00:07:28.720
So what Raime found there must have chilled him and corfirmed his fears about Nashandra.

00:07:29.000 --> 00:07:32.400
The entire tower had been enveloped by a black fog.

00:07:32.520 --> 00:07:34.600
It repelled any who came close,

00:07:34.600 --> 00:07:39.140
haunting suits of armor, and fighting off any soldiers who attempted to enter.

00:07:39.700 --> 00:07:42.320
However, Raime was not most soldiers.

00:07:42.320 --> 00:07:47.000
A stalwart warrior, Raime had the ability to expunge the black fog.

00:07:47.000 --> 00:07:51.820
He was strong, and tracked the black fog to its source at the base of the tower.

00:07:52.560 --> 00:07:58.360
Amongst the remnants of a past kingdom covered in ash was Nadalia, the Ashen Maiden.

00:07:58.720 --> 00:08:02.880
Nadalia arrived at this tower seeking a King, but was too late.

00:08:03.100 --> 00:08:08.540
The King she seeked had already sunk below the molten iron and his rule had passed.

00:08:09.380 --> 00:08:13.380
Dispirited, this Child of Dark made Brume Tower her home,

00:08:13.380 --> 00:08:16.900
in the place she might have ruled alongside her King.

00:08:17.400 --> 00:08:23.080
Perhaps Raime's original intent was to banish Nadalia, the Dark Queen of Brume Tower.

00:08:23.080 --> 00:08:29.060
If he could do this, then he could return with proof to his kingdom and make his King see the truth.

00:08:29.600 --> 00:08:33.840
At some point after entering Brume Tower though, this changed.

00:08:34.320 --> 00:08:38.580
Just like Raime, Nadalia was deprived of a King and kingdom.

00:08:38.580 --> 00:08:41.460
Perhaps they found some mutuality in this.

00:08:41.460 --> 00:08:48.460
Raime decided to trust this Child of Dark, allowing her to cling to his sword in her miasmic form.

00:08:49.100 --> 00:08:55.420
Raime was reborn, granted true purpose under a newfound mother, rather than a regal father.

00:08:56.180 --> 00:08:57.860
Which begs the question:

00:08:57.860 --> 00:09:04.200
Could such a Queen be evil? Or was Raime another victim of a Dark Queen's manipulation?

00:09:05.500 --> 00:09:09.020
After Raime left Drangleic, the kingdom collapsed.

00:09:09.020 --> 00:09:12.280
The Giants invaded, with revenge in their hearts

00:09:12.280 --> 00:09:16.320
and Nashandra took the throne, forcing Vendrick into hiding.

00:09:16.320 --> 00:09:22.580
Velstadt followed his King into the Undead Crypt, where he would guard him in darkness forever.

00:09:23.080 --> 00:09:27.800
Raime remained in Brume Tower, protecting the Ashen Maiden from harm.

00:09:28.200 --> 00:09:33.100
And then you come, seeking answers in empty kingdoms.

